What is the smallest positive integer that satisfies the following system of congruences?
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 2 \pmod{3} \\
x \equiv 4 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 5 \pmod{7}
\end{cases}
\]

Consider the system of equations:
\[ \left\{
\begin{aligned}
x^2 + yz &= xy + zy \\
xz + y^2 &= zx + wy \\
xz + yw &= w - 2 \\
\end{aligned}
\right. \]
where \(z\neq y\neq w\neq x\). How many different integer solutions \((x,y,z,w)\) exist?

\begin{align*}
\begin{cases}
x + \frac{1}{x} = 4 \\
x^2 + \frac{1}{x^2} = y \\
x^3 + \frac{1}{x^3} = z
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
Find $z$.。
